From 98c48c5867b3d52542988876f7e81f10d343b50b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:30:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qmi-firmware-update: don't match sysfs path in download mode
Organization: Wires

After a reset into download mode the modem may re-enumerate under
another root hub or host controller, e.g. usb4 -> usb3.  It then no
longer matches the sysfs path recorded before the reset, so
qmi-firmware-update never finds it.

Skip the sysfs path check when looking for a device in download mode.
With more than one modem in download mode at the same time, the first
one found is used.

Originally from the modem support donated by Avvero Pty Ltd.

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 src/qmi-firmware-update/qfu-helpers-udev.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/qmi-firmware-update/qfu-helpers-udev.c b/src/qmi-firmware-update/qfu-helpers-udev.c
index bda91061..cd25e0bc 100644
--- a/src/qmi-firmware-update/qfu-helpers-udev.c
+++ b/src/qmi-firmware-update/qfu-helpers-udev.c
@@ -364,7 +364,10 @@ device_matches (GUdevDevice          *device,
     if (!device_sysfs_path)
         goto out;
 
-    if (g_strcmp0 (device_sysfs_path, sysfs_path) != 0)
+    /* In download mode the device may re-enumerate on another root hub,
+     * e.g. usb4 -> usb3, so its sysfs path no longer matches */
+    if (mode != QFU_HELPERS_DEVICE_MODE_DOWNLOAD &&
+        g_strcmp0 (device_sysfs_path, sysfs_path) != 0)
         goto out;
 
     if (device_mode != mode)
